# MME-0114: the live visual-gate report is regenerated on every `npm run visual` run.
# Committing it guarantees the file in git describes whichever partial run happened last;
# the summary that matters is recorded in docs/internal/build-log.md, and CI uploads the
# JSON as a build artifact.
docs/internal/visual-checks/visual-gate-report.json

# MME-0116: screenshots are gate OUTPUT, not evidence. Every `npm run visual` re-renders
# them, so committing them made "run the suite before you commit" and "commit only your
# issue" contradict each other — MME-0123's run dirtied 242 tracked PNGs, none caused by
# its change, and the reflex that teaches (`git checkout -- docs/internal/visual-checks/`)
# is the same reflex that would hide a real rendering regression. Each gate's result.json
# and README.md stay committed: those are diffable. CI uploads the images.
#
# The exceptions below are declared in KEPT_VISUAL_ARTIFACTS in scripts/visual-gates.mjs
# with a reason and an owning issue; tests/visual-gate-integrity.test.mjs keeps the two
# lists in sync and rejects any other committed PNG.
docs/internal/visual-checks/**/*.png
!docs/internal/visual-checks/MME-0011.5/*.png
!docs/internal/visual-checks/MME-0100/before/*.png
